--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHY THIS FILE EXISTS WHEN IT SAYS THE SAME THING AS THE ONE ABOVE IT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Today these terms are the repository's terms. The file is here so that they do
not have to stay that way.

A signature is not the scanner. It is detection data: it can carry a string
lifted from a sample, it is rewritten on a different schedule from the engine,
and a project may one day want to say something about redistributing it -
attribution, or a restriction on training - that it would never say about the
code that reads it. Settled in the root LICENSE, that decision could not be
revisited without reopening every release already published under it.

So the seam is cut now, while it costs nothing, rather than when it is needed.
